TITLE:Work Uniform Spec
H1:M2 · Your work uniform (Day 8, Torres) <span class="draft">spec for approval</span>
SUB:Oily jobs make your uniform grubby faster; it looks a shade duller until you change at your wardrobe. Your own laundry is 0.60.7's (the wardrobe, the hamper, the washers); this adds only what grows from the job. Moved from Day 5 to Day 8 (the user's "puzzles earlier" change). Step 2, sub-block 24b. Plan Part 2, M2.
NAV:plain=In plain words|day=Day 8|why=Why it matters|grow=How it grows|b=Builder|save=Save|tests=Tests|ranges=Builds and keys

<section id="plain">
  <h2>In plain words</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Already in 0.60.7:</b> you change every morning at your wardrobe; after 5 days you take the hamper to a washer and back; if you don't change by 10:00 you're "in yesterday's clothes". No laundry duty.</li>
    <li><b>New:</b> some jobs are <b>oily</b> (ovens, the range, the extractor, the galley plant, cart docks, the lift, pumps, the main fan). After a couple of them your uniform is <b>grubby</b>: it looks a shade duller (a tint, nothing new drawn), and people notice.</li>
    <li><b>A shower doesn't clean it; a change does</b>: tap your wardrobe and change (it uses a clean outfit, even if you already changed today).</li>
    <li><b>Never a fail:</b> grubby costs a little hygiene and a remark or two, and matters on inspection mornings and at the officer ceremony.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="day">
  <h2>Day 8, Monday</h2>
  <p>Your first oily job turned in on Day 8 or later (from Day 8, oily jobs make you grubby): Torres catches you at the board or the tea corner. "You've got half the galley plant on you. Change before tea. Calder notices." A line on the Training page: "Your uniform: change after oily jobs."</p>
  <p class="note">Day 8's big new thing is your first incident with Calder (M6); this is its small one.</p>
</section>

<section id="why">
  <h2>Why it matters</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Hygiene:</b> grubby drains hygiene 1.5× (the same as "yesterday's clothes"; they don't add up).</li>
    <li><b>Remarks:</b> crew may say something (the existing path, <code>simNote('uniform')</code>), friends kindly, Calder briefly.</li>
    <li><b>The Thursday inspection</b> (M3) checks a clean uniform; <b>the officer ceremony</b> (Day 11, Step 3) does too.</li>
    <li><b>The washers wear with your loads</b>, as with the crew's, so you see their faults coming (and, later, service them).</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="grow">
  <h2>How it grows</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card"><b>Stage 1 · Grubby on oily jobs</b><span>As above.</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">Day 8</span></span></div>
    <div class="card"><b>Stage 2 · Service the washers</b><span>While your wash runs (30 ship minutes), a worn washer's service job is held for you right there: "While you wait." The washers are already real machines with panels.</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">after 2 washes</span><span class="tag new">optional</span></span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="note">From the Deck 2 suite (Senior Officer) your laundry is collected (0.60.7); your uniform is still yours to change.</p>
</section>

<section id="b" class="builder">
  <h2>For the builder (seat M1, sub-block 24b)</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Section</th><th>What</th><th>Owner</th></tr>
    <tr><td>15c clothes (0.60.7)</td><td><code>SHIP.player.clothes.grime</code> (0-1); <code>uniformState()</code> → <code>'clean' | 'yesterday' | 'grubby'</code>; a change while grubby always uses an outfit and sets grime 0; grubby drains hygiene like yesterday's clothes (max, not product)</td><td>the onboarding engineer (15c's owner, on call) or P with the lead's OK</td></tr>
    <tr><td>24b (new)</td><td>grime from jobs; the Day 8 moment; stage 2's held washer service</td><td>M1</td></tr>
    <tr><td>8 / 8b</td><td>the player's uniform tint: <code>playerUniformTint(k)</code>, k 0-1, multiplies the uniform's material colour toward grey (k = 1: 12% darker, 20% less saturated), through <code>col()</code>; the player only, no new material per frame (two cached materials, swapped)</td><td>performance (on call)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>17</td><td>nothing (the washers wear from <code>loads</code>, and your load already adds wear via <code>machineUse</code>)</td><td>—</td></tr>
    <tr><td>content</td><td>Torres's line (<code>train.m2</code>), remarks on <code>uniform: grubby</code></td><td>W</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Grime:</b> on <code>simNote('job', { step: 'turnin' })</code> for your job, from Day 8 (<code>SHIP.works.tr.m2</code> or the ladder's day): <code>OILY = new Set(['oven', 'range', 'extractor', 'galleyplant', 'cartdock', 'lift', 'pump', 'heatpump', 'fan', 'irrigation'])</code>; an oily repair or overhaul +.35, an oily service +.2, anything else +.05; grubby from .6 (so two oily repairs). Saved in 15c's <code>clothes</code>.</li>
    <li><b>The look:</b> <code>playerUniformTint(grime &gt;= .6 ? 1 : 0)</code> when the state changes (not every frame); <code>simNote('uniform', { state })</code> on each change of <code>uniformState()</code>.</li>
    <li><b>The Day 8 moment:</b> the ladder's small row <code>m2</code> (needs: an oily job turned in on Day 8+); Torres's line through a one-line meeting where he is (at the board or the tea corner within the next 90 ship minutes; else by Mail).</li>
    <li><b>Stage 2:</b> when you load a washer and another washer is worn (<code>machineState</code>), its service job is held for you (<code>j.until</code> = your wash's end + 10 minutes) with the title "While you wait: service Washer 3". Opens after 2 washes (<code>use.m2</code> counts washes from 15c's <code>simNote</code> or a 24b hook on "Take out").</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="save" class="builder">
  <h2>Save</h2>
  <ul><li><code>player.clothes.grime</code> (a number, 2 decimals; 15c reads it defensively, 0 if missing). <code>ship.works.use.m2</code>, <code>tr.m2</code>.</li></ul>
</section>

<section id="tests" class="builder">
  <h2>Tests</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b><code>mech_check</code></b> (24b): grime rises faster on oily jobs; two oily repairs make you grubby; a shower doesn't clear it, a change does (and uses an outfit); nothing before Day 8; stage 2's washer job held during your wash and released after.</li>
    <li><b><code>player_check</code></b>: hygiene drain grubby = yesterday's, not more; 0.60.7's clothes checks unchanged; the save of grime.</li>
    <li><b><code>intro_check</code></b>: the first week's laundry unchanged (nothing grubby before Day 8).</li>
    <li><b><code>cadet_test</code></b>: identical while clean (the tint only applies when grubby).</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="ranges" class="builder">
  <h2>Builds and keys</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Seat <b>M1</b>, branch <code>claude/mech-rounds</code>, builds <b>0.45.x</b>. Hash keys <b>862-863</b> (set aside; grime is deterministic and needs none today).</li>
    <li>Needs 0.60.7's 15c clothes in the base build.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
